QuestGuidance.Register("en",227,{
[7233]="7005B24E\n1\tTalk to Hórin\tHórin is waiting to proceed inside Thyrstáth. You should talk to Hórin.\n2\tFind the ice-giant chieftain\tYou should walk through Thyrstáth with Hórin until you find the ice-giant chieftain.\n3\tTalk to Hórin\tHórin is standing outside the throne-room in Thyrstáth. You should talk to Hórin.\n4\tListen to the conversation\tHórin is negotiating with the ice-giant chieftain. You should listen to the conversation.\n5\tBreak free of the dark force (total: 2)\tYou are held in place by a dark force!\n",
[7234]="70052D8F\n1\tListen to Legolas\tListen to Legolas.\n2\tLet Legolas tell his story\tLet Legolas tell his story.\n",
[7235]="70061BD2\n1\tTalk to Bregoleth in her memory of Caras Gelebren\tBregoleth weaves a tale of Caras Gelebren as it appeared during the years she lived there during the Second Age of Middle-earth.\n2\tFollow Bregoleth and listen as she weaves her tale\tBregoleth weaves a tale of Caras Gelebren in the Second Age of Middle-earth.\n3\tTalk to Bregoleth in her memory of Caras Gelebren\tBregoleth weaves a tale of Caras Gelebren as it appeared during the years she lived there during the Second Age of Middle-earth.\n4\tListen as Bregoleth weaves her tale\tBregoleth weaves a tale of Caras Gelebren in the Second Age of Middle-earth.\n5\tTalk to Bregoleth in her memory of Caras Gelebren\tBregoleth weaves a tale of Caras Gelebren as it appeared during the years she lived there during the Second Age of Middle-earth.\n6\tListen as Bregoleth weaves her tale\tBregoleth weaves a tale of Caras Gelebren in the Second Age of Middle-earth.\n7\tTalk to Bregoleth in her memory of Caras Gelebren\tBregoleth weaves a tale of Caras Gelebren as it appeared during the years she lived there during the Second Age of Middle-earth.\n8\tTalk to Bregoleth in her memory of Caras Gelebren\tBregoleth weaves a tale of Caras Gelebren as it appeared during the years she lived there during the Second Age of Middle-earth.\n9\tListen as Bregoleth weaves her tale\tBregoleth weaves a tale of Caras Gelebren in the Second Age of Middle-earth.\n10\tTalk to Bregoleth in her memory of Caras Gelebren\tBregoleth weaves a tale of Caras Gelebren as it appeared during the years she lived there during the Second Age of Middle-earth.\n11\tTalk to Bregoleth in a place of unimaginable evil\tBregoleth weaves a tale of Caras Gelebren as it appeared during the years she lived there during the Second Age of Middle-earth.\n12\tLeave Bregoleth behind to hear the end of her tale, which lies ahead within the Mountain of Fire\tBregoleth speaks of a place she has never seen, a place of unimaginable evil: the inside of Orodruin, the Mountain of Fire in the Black Land of Mordor.\n",
[7236]="700539EA\n1\tTalk to Glorfindel in the tunnel of Halroth\tGlorfindel is in the tunnel of Halroth, prepared to fight through the dark passage to Barad-dûr itself.\n2\tTalk to Glorfindel in the tunnel of Halroth\tGlorfindel is in the tunnel of Halroth, prepared to fight through the dark passage to Barad-dûr itself.\n3\tTalk to Glorfindel in the tunnel of Halroth\tGlorfindel is in the tunnel of Halroth, prepared to fight through the dark passage to Barad-dûr itself.\n4\tTalk to Lendelen inside Barad-dûr\tNow that you have passed beyond the wall of Barad-dûr with the Bright Company, Lendelen wishes to speak to you.\n5\tClimb the spiral stair and speak with an Elf of the Bright Company outside the upper chambers\tLendelen wants you to climb the spiral stair to the upper floors of the tower, where other Elves of the Bright Company will join you.\n6\tFollow the Bright Company into the upper chambers of the tower\tLendelen and Glorfindel have rejoined you atop the stair, and now their mission, and yours, must be completed.\n7\tTalk to Glorfindel in Barad-dûr\tThe Bright Company stands against the Nazgûl in a high chamber of Barad-dûr, but the mission of Glorfindel and Lendelen remains higher still.\n8\tFollow Glorfindel and Lendelen to the chamber of the Vandassar, and stand with them\tThe Bright Company stands against the Nazgûl in a high chamber of Barad-dûr, but the mission of Glorfindel and Lendelen remains higher still.\n9\tTalk to Sauron\tYou have come face to face with Sauron in an upper chamber of Barad-dûr, and must distract the Dark Lord from his real danger.\n10\tStand with Glorfindel and Lendelen\tThe mission of the Bright Company all comes down to this moment, high in the chamber of the Vandassar.\n11\tFollow Glorfindel and escape from the tower!\tLendelen has successfully broken Sauron's hold upon the Vandassar, and now you must escape from the tower! This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n12\tTalk to Glorfindel in Barad-dûr\tGlorfindel has halted, waiting for Lendelen.\n13\tListen to the words of Glorfindel\tGlorfindel has concluded his tale of the last glorious mission of the Bright Company, in which Sauron's control over the Vandassar was broken.\n14\tTalk to Glorfindel on Tol Send\tGlorfindel stands on Tol Send, ready to conclude his tale.\n15\tListen to the words of Glorfindel\tGlorfindel stands on Tol Send, ready to conclude his tale.\n16\tTalk to Gandalf on Tol Send\tGandalf stands on Tol Send, the events of the past newly-awakened in him.\n",
[7237]="70052CD0\n1\tTalk to Langhár\tLanghár is ready to explain her plan to enter the goblin hideout. You should talk to Langhár.\n2\tWave at Langhár when in position\030Get into position next to the village gate\tLanghár has asked you to get closer to the cave entrance before she alerts the goblins. You should get into position, and then wave at Langhár to give the signal.\n3\tEnter the cave behind the village\tLanghár has drawn the attention of the goblins in Waldfast. You should sneak behind them and find the cave she mentioned.\n4\tInvestigate the cave\tYou should investigate the cave to find evidence of why the goblins are here and how many they number.\n5\tEavesdrop upon the Great Goblin\tYou have found the Great Goblin and a large number of goblins loyal to him. You should listen to him speak to his followers to see what you can learn.\n6\tReturn to Langhár\tYou have learned much about the Great Goblin's situation. You should return to Langhár and tell her this new information.\n",
[7238]="70032BF0\n1\tTalk to Dómárr\tDómárr and Reinn can be found in the Great Hall of Durin.\n2\tListen to Reinn and Dómárr\tDómárr and Reinn can be found in the Great Hall of Durin.\n3\tTalk to Dómárr\tDómárr and Reinn can be found in the Great Hall of Durin.\n4\tListen to the dwarves' discussion\tDómárr and Reinn can be found in the Great Hall of Durin.\n5\tTalk to Dómárr\tDómárr can be found in the Great Hall of Durin. You should speak with Dómárr.\n",
[7239]="7006F398\n1\tTalk to Ulishár in the back-stage chambers\tUlishár stands with you in the back-stage chambers of the performance hall in Emax Dûl.\n2\tTalk to Satagêra by the rear entrance to the stage\tSatagêra stands by the doorway leading to the stage.\n3\tWait for your cue to arrive, and then run up the stairs on the right side\tSatagêra has told you to wait for your moment to run onto the stage.\n4\tRun up the stairs and deliver your line\tYour big moment has arrived! Run up the stairs on the right side of the stage and stand by the door to the west hallway.\n5\tWait for your next cue\tNow you must wait for your second cue. Once Mashkânu says 'Well?' you must faint... but not before!\n6\tFaint at the sight of the impressive Mûmak\tFaint at the sight of the impressive Mûmak.\n7\tSlip inside the west hallway while the audience is distracted\tNow is your chance! Slip inside the hallway while the audience is distracted.\n8\tTalk to Ulishár in the hallway west of the stage\tUlishár has joined you in the hallway west of the stage, in the belly of Emax Dûl.\n9\tRead the papers in the Lord's Study\tThe papers in the Lord's Study may provide the information you seek. Search them and learn what you can!\n10\tRead more of the papers in the Lord's Study\tThe papers in the Lord's Study may provide the information you seek. Search them and learn what you can!\n11\tListen to Ulishár read the unsent letter he has found\tUlishár has found an unsent letter in the Lord's Study.\n12\tTalk to Ulishár in the Lord's Study\tUlishár wishes to speak with you in the Lord's Study.\n13\tJoin the other performers on the stage as the play comes to an end\tThe play is almost over, and you should join the other performers on the stage.\n14\tTake your bow\030Join the other performers on the stage\tTake your bow with the other performers.\n15\tReturn to the rooms backstage and wait for the rest of Têrkar's Travellers\tYou learned what you came for, and should now return to the rooms backstage to wait for the rest of Têrkar's Travellers.\n",
[7240]="70020DA4\n1\tDefeat the Grey King\tFind and defeat the Grey King in its lair.\n",
[7241]="70059AF3\n1\tTalk to Durin\tDurin cannot understand why his namesake would have trusted Mótsog with the lordship of Gundabad.\n2\tListen to the tale of Mótsog\tMótsog has agreed to speak of the treachery for which he is remembered.\n3\tTalk to Mótsog\tMótsog weaves to you the tale of his treachery's foundation.\n4\tListen to the tale of Mótsog\tMótsog weaves to you the tale of his treachery's foundation.\n5\tTalk to Mótsog\tMótsog weaves to you the tale of his treachery's foundation.\n6\tListen to the tale of Mótsog\tMótsog weaves to you the tale of his treachery's foundation.\n7\tTalk to Mótsog\tMótsog weaves to you the tale of his treachery's foundation.\n8\tListen to the tale of Mótsog\tMótsog weaves to you the tale of his treachery's foundation.\n9\tTalk to Mótsog\tMótsog weaves to you the tale of his treachery's foundation.\n",
[7242]="7000E37E\n1\tTalk to Yrjänä\tAccompany Yrjänä to meet with the emissary of Angmar.\n2\tYrjänä and the Elders of the Lossoth are to meet with the emissary from Angmar.\t\n",
[7243]="70045E59\n1\tTalk to Aragorn\tAragorn is by Faramir's bedside in the Houses of Healing.\n2\tRemain alert in the event you are needed\tAragorn is by Faramir's bedside in the Houses of Healing.\n3\tFollow Aragorn to Éowyn's bedside\tFaramir has recovered, and now Aragorn goes to see if Éowyn's condition has improved.\n4\tRemain alert in the event you are needed\tAragorn is by Éowyn's bedside in the Houses of Healing.\n5\tWalk to Merry's bedside\tAragorn has gone to Merry's bedside to see if his work has aided the hobbit's recovery.\n6\tRemain alert in the event you are needed\tAragorn is by Merry's bedside in the Houses of Healing.\n7\tTalk to Merry\tMerry is still in bed, but he seems to be recovering.\n",
[7244]="7004E17D\n1\tTalk to Postmaster Proudfoot in the Quick Post\tPostmaster Proudfoot is in the Quick Post, and he says he can show you the letters that might hold what you seek.\n2\tFollow Postmaster Proudfoot to the Quick Post Cellar\tPostmaster Proudfoot has offered to show you the old letters to Halson Cleary, which have been kept in the cellar of the Quick Post for as long as he can remember.\n3\tRead one of the forgotten letters\tPiles of forgotten letters to Halson Cleary can be found in the Quick Post cellar.\n4\tStudy the letters for some clue to the haunting of Wistmead\tPiles of forgotten letters to Halson Cleary can be found in the Quick Post cellar.\n5\tRead one of the forgotten letters\tPiles of forgotten letters to Halson Cleary can be found in the Quick Post cellar.\n6\tStudy the letters for some clue to the haunting of Wistmead\tPiles of forgotten letters to Halson Cleary can be found in the Quick Post cellar.\n7\tRead one of the forgotten letters\tPiles of forgotten letters to Halson Cleary can be found in the Quick Post cellar.\n8\tStudy the letters for some clue to the haunting of Wistmead\tPiles of forgotten letters to Halson Cleary can be found in the Quick Post cellar.\n9\tRead one of the forgotten letters\tPiles of forgotten letters to Halson Cleary can be found in the Quick Post cellar.\n10\tStudy the letters for some clue to the haunting of Wistmead\tPiles of forgotten letters to Halson Cleary can be found in the Quick Post cellar.\n11\tRead one of the forgotten letters\tPiles of forgotten letters to Halson Cleary can be found in the Quick Post cellar.\n12\tStudy the letters for some clue to the haunting of Wistmead\tPiles of forgotten letters to Halson Cleary can be found in the Quick Post cellar.\n13\tTalk to Postmaster Proudfoot in the cellar of the Quick Post\tPostmaster Proudfoot has returned to the cellar of the Quick Post and is waiting to hear what you have learned.\n",
[7245]="70010046\n1\tSearch for Laerdan's breastplate\tSearch through Dolendath for some sign of Laerdan's breastplate.\n2\tSearch for the source of the strange laughter\tA strange voice beckoned you forwards. Discover its source.\n3\tDefeat Goeolgúr\tYour search for the source of the strange laughter led you to a gaunt-man. This vile creature must be defeated.\n",
[7246]="7004E63F\n1\tTalk to Khîl in his father's house\tKhîl has brought you to his father's house. He is consumed with worry about something he discovered there.\n2\tListen to Khîl's explanation\tKhîl has brought you to his father's house. He is consumed with worry about something he discovered there.\n3\tExamine Painting\030Examine Ore Barrow\030Examine Desk\030Examine Bed\030Examine Table\030Use Bench\030Use Table\tKhîl has asked you to search his father's house for some means of opening the secret door he discovered.\n4\tExamine Painting\030Examine Ore Barrow\030Examine Desk\030Examine Bed\030Use Crates\030Examine Table\030Use Bench\030Use Table\tKhîl has asked you to search his father's house for some means of opening the secret door he discovered.\n5\tReturn to Khîl\tKhîl has asked you to search his father's house for some means of opening the secret door he discovered.\n6\tTalk to Khîl by the secret door\tKhîl is standing in front of the secret door, but it remains closed.\n7\tExamine Open Chest\tKhîl has asked you to search his father's house for some means of opening the secret door he discovered.\n8\tTalk to Khîl by the secret door\tKhîl stands by the secret door, studying the runes that appeared on its face.\n9\tHelp Khîl discover the words that will open the door\tKhîl is standing in front of the secret door, trying to learn the words that will open it.\n10\tTalk to Khîl outside the secret door\tKhîl has discovered the word that opens the secret door: Vóin, the name of his great-great-great-grandfather.\n11\tExplore the hidden chamber with Khîl\tKhîl has discovered the word that opens the secret door: Vóin, the name of his great-great-great-grandfather. Now he wishes to explore the chamber.\n12\tTalk to Khîl inside the hidden chamber\tKhîl is inside the hidden chamber in his father's house.\n",
[7247]="7000016B\n1\tSpeak to the Blackwold guard\tSpeak to the Blackwold guard. If your ruse is successful, he should give you access to the hideout. Toradan sent you to Skunkwood's hideout to rescue Amdir and put an end to the Blackwolds' mischief.\n2\tTalk to William Skunkwood\tSkunkwood resides somewhere within the hideout. You have tricked your way into the Blackwolds' hideout. Now you must find Skunkwood and speak with him to learn the whereabouts of Amdir.\n3\tSearch for Amdir\tAmdir lies in the dungeons at the far end of the Blackwold hideout. Skunkwood told you that Amdir was locked away and that what was happening to him seemed unnatural. You should find Amdir quickly.\n4\tTalk to Amdir\tYou have discovered Amdir and found that he has partially transformed into a wraith. He stopped raving at the sight of you, so perhaps there is still some hope for him.\n5\tSpeak with the old prisoner\tAn old woman in the back of the cell that held Amdir called to you for help. You should help her escape. Whatever is happening to Amdir, it has driven him completely mad, and he is far more powerful than he first seemed. His deafening scream momentarily stunned you and threw open his cell door.\n6\tAid Toradan\tTry to help Toradan defeat Amdir. As neared the entrance of the Blackwold Hideout, you encountered Toradan and Amdir.\n7\tSpeak to Toradan\tAfter helping Sara Oakheart out of the Blackwold hideout, Toradan entered and saw what had become of Amdir. Seeing his kinsman too far gone to help, Toradan attempted to slay him, but was instead himself stricken down. You should speak with Toradan before he perishes.\n8\tTalk to Sara Oakheart\tToradan spoke about Amdir trying to kill the other Rangers and asked you to speak with Constable Underhill about a message he sent to someone named Tanglerush. Before leaving the hideout, however, you should speak to Sara Oakheart again to see if she needs any further help.\n",
[7248]="7002FA0F\n1\tCome to the aid of the hobbits!\tThe hobbits Meriadoc and Peregrin are in danger! You have to come to their aid!\n2\tDefeat the Uruk that threatens the hobbits!\tAn Uruk threatens the hobbits!\n3\tTalk to Meriadoc\tMeriadoc and Peregrin need your help. They are not safe of the Uruks yet!\n4\tBlow the Horn of Gondor to summon aid!\tThe number of the Uruks is overwhelming! You need aid! Blow the Horn of Gondor!\n5\tTalk to Peregrin\tMeriadoc and Peregrin need your help. They are not safe of the Uruks yet!\n6\tBlow the Horn of Gondor to summon aid!\tThe number of the Uruks is overwhelming! You need aid! Blow the Horn of Gondor!\n7\tExamine the dying Uruk in the middle of the glade\tYou have to protect the hobbits, at any cost!\n8\tDefend the hobbits\tThe Uruks are closing in...\n9\tDefend the hobbits\tYou have done what you could, Boromir.\n",
[7249]="700216AB\n1\tTalk to Haerdor\tIn the year 1975 of the Third Age, a party of Dúnedain led by the brothers Laegened and Haerdor travelled north into Forochel to reclaim the relics left behind in the flight from the wreck of Fornost. Haerdor has scouted ahead and wishes to speak with you.\n2\tDefeat winter-worms in the pass to Forochel (total: 6)\tWorms can be found on the rise to the east of Haerdor. Your brother Haerdor has asked you to use your stealthy abilities to clear the path ahead of worms.\n3\tTalk to Haerdor down the hill to the west\tHaerdor is waiting to hear that the winter-worms have been cleared from the pass.\n4\tListen to Candaith's narrative continue\tIt is the year Nineteen Seventy-five of the Third Age, and the journey of Laegened and Haerdor has brought them to the shores of the Ice Bay in search of their king. Haerdor has arrived on the shores of the Ice Bay, beholding the broken ship that was sent to rescue Arvedui. He waits to speak with you.\n5\tTalk to Haerdor\tIt is the year Nineteen Seventy-five of the Third Age, and the journey of Laegened and Haerdor has brought them to the shores of the Ice Bay in search of their king. Haerdor is waiting to speak with you on the shores of the Ice Bay.\n6\tTalk to Hasikkä\tHasikkä, the chieftain of the Lossoth, is waiting to speak with you.\n7\tTalk to Haerdor\tHaerdor is waiting to speak with you.\n8\tListen to Candaith's narrative continue\tIt is the year Twenty-nine Thirty of the Third Age, and Arador, the Chieftain of the Dúnedain, has not returned from the Troll-height, where he adventured to maintain the safety of his people. Glangon fears the worst.\n9\tTalk to Glangon\tIt is the year Twenty-nine Thirty of the Third Age, and Arador, the Chieftain of the Dúnedain, has not returned from the Troll-height, where he adventured to maintain the safety of his people. Glangon fears the worst. Glangon is waiting to speak with you below the Troll-height.\n10\tThe Hill-trolls of the Ettenmoors seized Arador, the Chieftain of the Dúnedain and must be defeated if he is to be rescued.\t\n11\tTalk to Glangon\tThe Hill-trolls have been defeated, but it is too late for Arador, Chieftain of the Dúnedain.\n12\tListen to Candaith's narrative continue\tIt is the year Twenty-nine Fifty-six of the Third Age, and Aragorn son of Arathorn plans to begin the great journeys by which he would come to know the world. He is waiting to speak with you, for he wishes to bid farewell before he travels into the south-lands.\n13\tTalk to Aragorn\tIt is the year Twenty-nine Fifty-six of the Third Age, and Aragorn son of Arathorn plans to begin the great journeys by which he would come to know the world. But first he must bid farewell to the friends of his childhood.\n14\tListen to the exchange between Aragorn and the old man\tAragorn and Túgonn have encountered an old man on the road through the Dimrill Dale.\n15\tTalk to Gandalf the Grey\tGandalf the Grey is waiting to speak with you.\n16\tTalk to Aragorn\tAragorn is waiting to speak with you.\n",
[7250]="700010AA\n1\tDefeat Yellowfang\tYellowfang is somewhere within the Old Forest. Gytha Lainey has tasked you with defeating Yellowfang, a deadly wolf that stalks the Old Forest. She warned you that Yellowfang is cunning, and you will need to devise some way to lure her out of hiding.\n2\tTalk to Gytha Lainey\tGytha Lainey is waiting for you somewhere in the Old Forest. Gytha will be both pleased and surprised to know that you have defeated Yellowfang.\n",
[7251]="70057E68\n1\tTalk to Léothred\tTalk to Léothred.\n2\tListen to Léothred's tale\tListen to Léothred's tale.\n",
[7252]="7002D45A\n1\tFind and talk to Quick-wit Culver\tQuick-wit Culver is inside the Infiltrators' Hideout. You need to see if you can stop the infiltrators' surprise.\n2\tFind and talk to Twisted Garrett\tTwisted Garrett is in the Infiltrators' Hideout. You need to see if you can stop the infiltrators' surprise.\n3\tTalk to Artie Root\tArtie Root is in the Infiltrators' Hideout.\n4\tTalk to Quick-wit Culver\tQuick-wit Culver is in the Infiltrators' Hideout.\n5\tTalk to Sig Mandrake\tSig Mandrake is in the Infiltrators' Hideout.\n6\tTalk to Artie Root\tArtie Root is in the Infiltrators' Hideout.\n",
[7253]="7005AF69\n1\tTalk to Scoutmaster Ausma\tAusma is pleased with your progress so far.\n2\tFollow Scout-master Ausma\tYou should follow Ausma.\n3\tEnter Shakhajât\t\n4\tTalk to Scout-master Ausma\tAusma is continuing to explore, and will need your help.\n5\tListen to the conversation\tYou should eavesdrop and see what can be learned.\n",
[7254]="70017B89\n1\tSearch for the innermost chamber\tSearch for the innermost chamber of the secret hall -- following the clues may help find it faster.\n2\tExamine the weapon closely\tInvestigate the weapon on the dais within the innermost chamber.\n",
[7255]="7004A1D7\n1\tTalk to Ingold\tTalk to Ingold.\n2\tGet closer so that you may overhear the conversation\tGet closer so that you may overhear the conversation.\n3\tListen to the conversation\tListen to the conversation.\n4\tListen to the conversation\tListen to the conversation. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n5\tConfront Dulgabêth's servants and retrieve the Ithil-stone\tConfront Dulgabêth's servants and retrieve the Ithil-stone.\n6\tLet events transpire\tLet events transpire.\n7\tDefeat Dulgabêth's servants.\t\n8\tTalk to Ingold\tTalk to Ingold.\n9\tFollow Ingold\tFollow Ingold.\n10\tTalk to Ingold\tTalk to Ingold.\n",
[7256]="70037796\n1\tTalk to Agelwyn\tAgelwyn can be found in the refugees' hiding spot north of Marton. You should help Agelwyn lead her people to Helm's Deep.\n2\tListen to Agelwyn\tAgelwyn can be found in the refugees' hiding spot north of Marton. You should help Agelwyn lead her people to Helm's Deep.\n3\tSpeak with Agelwyn\tAgelwyn can be found in the refugees' hiding spot north of Marton. You should help Agelwyn lead her people to Helm's Deep.\n4\tSpeak with Agelwyn\tAgelwyn and her party are by the river-bank in the southern Westfold. You should speak with Agelwyn.\n5\tKeep the people of Marton safe\tAgelwyn and her party are travelling along the river-bank towards Helm's Deep. You should keep the people of Marton safe as they travel.\n6\tFollow Agelwyn\tFollow Agelwyn and keep her people safe.\n7\tMourn the slaughtered innocents\tYou should mourn the refugees.\n8\tSpeak with Agelwyn\tYou should speak with Agelwyn.\n",
[7257]="70037DBC\n1\tTalk to Théoden outside Edoras\tThéoden is outside Edoras, ready to ride to war.\n2\tTalk to Éomer outside Edoras\tÉomer is outside Edoras, with the great host that has assembled to ride with Théoden.\n3\tTalk to Legolas outside Edoras\030Talk to Aragorn outside Edoras\030Talk to Gimli outside Edoras\tAragorn, Legolas, and Gimli are by the side of the river outside Edoras, waiting for the host to depart.\n4\tTalk to Théoden among the host\tThéoden is outside Edoras, among the host that plans to ride to Isengard.\n5\tFind and talk to Gléowine outside Edoras\tGléowine is somewhere outside Edoras. Théoden has asked for you to bring Gléowine before him.\n6\tListen to Théoden issue commands before the host\tThéoden has called Gléowine before him.\n7\tTalk to Théoden before the host\tThéoden wishes to speak with you before the host departs.\n",
[7258]="70047292\n1\tTalk to Hrostyr\tHrostyr, the personal guard of King Thorin, will bring you to see him.\n2\tWait with Bósi for your audience with King Thorin\tYou are waiting for an audience with King Thorin.\n3\tKnock the helm from Dómor's hand before he gives it to Thorin\tSomething is not right! You have to stop Thorin from wearing that helm!\n4\tRemain on your guard and protect the king from danger\tA sensation of great evil emanates from the fallen helm!\n5\tDefeat Dómor\tKing Thorin has commanded you to keep Dómor from escaping.\n6\tRemain on your guard for further danger\tEvil has come to the Lonely Mountain, and the dwarves fight to defend their home.\n",
[7259]="70047298\n1\tTalk to Imrahil before the gate of Minas Tirith\tPrince Imrahil of Dol Amroth is before the gate of the White City, waiting to speak with you.\n2\tPrince Imrahil told you to find a good place to stand among the townsfolk on the right side as you approach the city.\t\n3\tWitness events as they transpire before the city\tThe Host of the West has come to the gate of Minas Tirith, and Faramir, Steward of Gondor, greets Aragorn outside the city.\n4\tCheer for the king and for Gondor\tAfter so long, Gondor at last has a king again.\n5\tGondor has a king again!\tAfter so long, Gondor at last has a king again.\n",
[7260]="70037096\n1\tSecure the windows and door\tCheck the windows and doors to make sure they are secured.\n2\tDefend Lúfa against the White Hand's hirelings\tDefend Lúfa against the White Hand's hirelings.\n3\tCheck the corpse of the brigand leader for evidence\tCheck the corpse of the brigand leader for evidence.\n4\tTalk to Lúfa in Ordlac's house\tLúfa is at Ordlac's house in Oserley. Speak with Lúfa and make sure that she is unharmed.\n",
[7261]="70036A34\n1\tObserve Théoden's encounter upon the road\tThéoden and his company are at the head of the line of horsemen in the Westfold. You should observe this memory of Éomer's by approaching Théoden.\n2\tListen to Ceorl's address to the company\tCeorl had much to say of the the events at the Fords of Isen. You should listen to Ceorl's address to the company.\n3\tHear what Céorl has to say\tCeorl had much to say of the the events at the Fords of Isen. You should listen to Ceorl's address to the company.\n4\tListen to Ceorl and the King\tCeorl had much to say of the the events at the Fords of Isen. You should listen to Ceorl's address to the company.\n",
[7262]="70059B14\n1\tTalk to Mótsog\tYou have been tasked with escorting Mótsog to the peak above Gundabad, where the last of the Greymauls will confront Hrímil Frost-heart.\n2\tTalk to Mótsog on the slope\tYou have been tasked with escorting Mótsog to the peak above Gundabad, where the last of the Greymauls will confront Hrímil Frost-heart.\n3\tTalk to Mótsog on the slope\tYou have been tasked with escorting Mótsog to the peak above Gundabad, where the last of the Greymauls will confront Hrímil Frost-heart.\n4\tTalk to Mótsog beneath the peak\tYou have been tasked with escorting Mótsog to the peak above Gundabad, where the last of the Greymauls will confront Hrímil Frost-heart.\n5\tConfront Hrímil Frost-heart\tYou have been tasked with escorting Mótsog to the peak above Gundabad, where the last of the Greymauls will confront Hrímil Frost-heart.\n6\tDefeat Ailgar and Rúvaran\tTwo leaders of the Angmarim have blocked your way up the slope to Hrímil Frost-heart, and they must be defeated if Mótsog is to reach the dragon.\n7\tConfront Hrímil Frost-heart\tYou have been tasked with escorting Mótsog to the peak above Gundabad, where the last of the Greymauls will confront Hrímil Frost-heart.\n8\tDefeat Gorgar the Ruthless\tGorgar has succumbed to the voice of the dragon. He must be defeated if Mótsog is to face Hrímil Frost-heart.\n9\tStand with Mótsog\tAs the sun sets behind distant hills, Mótsog's time on this world draws near its end. The dragon still lives.\n",
[7263]="7000114F\n1\tTalk to Gimli\tSpeak with Gimli to begin your foray into the dwarf-keep. The dwarf-keep in the pass of Gabilazan might be both the last hiding-place of the Dourhands led by Skorgrím and the Nazgûl you have pursued through the Trollshaws and into the Misty Mountains.\n2\tTalk to Gimli\tSpeak with Gimli to continue your foray into the dwarf-keep. The dwarf-keep in the pass of Gabilazan might be both the last hiding-place of the Dourhands led by Skorgrím and the Nazgûl you have pursued through the Trollshaws and into the Misty Mountains.\n3\tTalk to Gimli\tSpeak with Gimli to continue your foray into the dwarf-keep. The dwarf-keep in the pass of Gabilazan might be both the last hiding-place of the Dourhands led by Skorgrím and the Nazgûl you have pursued through the Trollshaws and into the Misty Mountains.\n4\tConfront the Nazgûl and Skorgrím\tYou have made your way deep into the dwarf-keep. It is nearly time to confront the Nazgûl and Skorgrím. Speak with Gimli to begin the final battle. The dwarf-keep in the pass of Gabilazan might be both the last hiding-place of the Dourhands led by Skorgrím and the Nazgûl you have pursued through the Trollshaws and into the Misty Mountains.\n5\tTalk to Gimli\tGimli is standing in the courtyard of the keep of Gabilazan. You have successfully defeated Skorgrím Dourhand, but the significance of his death is still uncertain.\n",
[7264]="70060574\n1\tTalk to Himeinior\tHimeinior has agreed to help Ravaedron with his latest scheme, and is waiting to speak with you.\n2\tTalk to Ravaedron\tRavaedron has finished whatever he was doing, and is now ready to thank you for your help.\n3\tTalk to Ravaedron outside Fernbrake Cot\tYou have come with Ravaedron to Fernbrake Cot.\n4\tKnock on the door to Fernbrake Cot\tRavaedron has asked you to knock on the door to Fernbrake Cot.\n5\tWeather the storm of the Stagshorns' displeasure with Ravaedron\tYou have drawn the unenviable task of weathering the storm of the Stagshorns' displeasure with Ravaedron.\n6\tFollow Ravaedron\tRavaedron has invited you and the Stagshorns to follow him around the side of Fernbrake Cot.\n",
